{
  "_comment": [
    "THE SHORT CODE EACH LAYER IS WRITTEN AS IN A MAP LINK, for the whole fleet.",
    "A shared link names its layers by these codes (#p=41.8825,-87.6285&l=wd,cg)",
    "rather than by their ids (#point=41.88250,-87.62850&layers=ward,congress),",
    "which roughly halves a typical link and shrinks its QR code. Adopted",
    "2026-10-09; every link written before then keeps working, because the app",
    "reads both forms.",
    "",
    "A CODE IS PERMANENT. A link already shared carries it, in messages, posts",
    "and print nobody can recall, so a code is never changed, never deleted and",
    "never given to another layer. A layer that is retired KEEPS its entry here.",
    "scripts/generate_metro_files.py --check fails when an entry present at the",
    "base of a change has been removed or changed.",
    "",
    "One code per layer id and one id per code, across every instance, so a",
    "layer two apps share (county, congress, zip-code) has one code everywhere.",
    "A code is a lowercase letter followed by one or two lowercase letters or",
    "digits, and never equals a layer id, because the app also accepts a full",
    "id in the same list. A NEW LAYER NEEDS AN ENTRY HERE: the generator refuses",
    "a worksheet layer with no code, and emits each instance's own codes as",
    "LAYER_CODES into that instance's metro-config region."
  ],
